{
  "result": "If I could change one thing, I wouldn't make everyone agree with each other \u2014 I think disagreement is where a lot of good ideas come from.\n\nI'd make it impossible to dehumanize another person.\n\nImagine if, in the moment you were about to dismiss, mock, exploit, or hurt someone, you automatically experienced a flash of their inner life as vividly as your own \u2014 their fears, memories, embarrassments, hopes, the people waiting for them at home. Not as information you could ignore, but as something you *felt* was real.\n\nYou could still compete. You could still argue, set boundaries, vote differently, or think someone is completely wrong. But you couldn't comfortably treat them as a stereotype, an avatar, an enemy, or a statistic.\n\nSo much cruelty and indifference depends on distance. Wars are easier when the other side is faceless. Online pile-ons are easier when there's no person behind the username. Bad policy is easier when the people affected are abstract numbers. Even everyday unkindness usually requires forgetting, for a second, that the other person has a whole life unfolding from inside them, just like you do.\n\nTake away that forgetting, and I suspect a lot would change on its own \u2014 not into perfect harmony, but into something more honest and less needlessly cruel.\n\nWhat would your one change be?",
